sequenceDiagram
  participant User
  participant Native as NativeBranchStore
  participant Meta as Metadata Store
  participant Data as Data Stores

  User->>Native: merge_apply(source, target)
  Native->>Meta: read source/target/base branch heads
  Native->>Meta: find source/target/base segments
  Native->>Data: compute changed keys and conflicts
  Native->>Meta: reserve branch transaction commit<br/>allocate merge + continuation segments
  Native->>Data: write merged rows into merge segment
  Native->>Meta: atomically update target.current_segment_id<br/>old target -> continuation
  Native->>Meta: delete commit record
  Native-->>User: MergeResult(applied=n)

  Note over Meta,Data: Readers see either old target segment<br/>or continuation segment that sees merge rows,<br/>never partial merge.
